uest is processed\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An authenticated parking administrator has authorized access to another employee's record\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.5\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the response status is successful and the returned fields contain the record permitted by the administrator's permissions\",\n     \"when\": \"the administrator retrieves that record\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee signs in, the Folio3 parking web app shall require the signed-in Folio3 Google identity to match the corporate email used for that employee's self-service profile lookup, restrict employee and vehicle data to that employee, and permit administrators to access other employee records only under their authorized permissions, while retrieving employee identity from the corporate directory and parking assignments and registered vehicle details from the administrator-maintained roster initially loaded from existing records.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"Q-4\",\n    \"Q-11\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An employee without dedicated parking has no registered vehicle\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the response rejects the claim and the response field identifies vehicle registration as required\",\n     \"when\": \"the employee attempts a claim before registering a plate\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An employee submits a plate with optional make, model, and color\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the returned vehicle record contains the plate and submitted optional fields, and the plate is eligible for a parking claim\",\n     \"when\": \"the employee registers the vehicle\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An employee without a registered vehicle opens the first-login flow\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.3\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"the s